## Securing WebSocket Communication

## 1. Always Use WSS (Encrypted)

```javascript
// ❌ Plaintext
const ws = new WebSocket('ws://api.example.com/ws');

// ✅ TLS encrypted
const ws = new WebSocket('wss://api.example.com/ws');
```

WSS uses TLS over port 443, same as HTTPS.

## 2. Authentication on Handshake

```javascript
// Option A: Token in URL (works but visible in logs)
const ws = new WebSocket(`wss://api.example.com/ws?token=${jwt}`);

// Server: validate before upgrading
server.on('upgrade', (req, socket, head) => {
  const token = new URL(req.url, 'http://x').searchParams.get('token');
  if (!verifyJWT(token)) { socket.destroy(); return; }
  wss.handleUpgrade(req, socket, head, (ws) => wss.emit('connection', ws, req));
});

// Option B: First message after connect (can use cookie)
ws.onopen = () => ws.send(JSON.stringify({ type: 'auth', token: jwt }));
```

## 3. Validate Origin Header

```javascript
const ALLOWED_ORIGINS = new Set(['https://app.example.com']);

server.on('upgrade', (req, socket, head) => {
  if (!ALLOWED_ORIGINS.has(req.headers.origin)) {
    socket.write('HTTP/1.1 403 Forbidden\r\n\r\n');
    socket.destroy();
    return;
  }
});
```

## 4. Rate Limiting and Input Validation

```javascript
const msgCount = new Map();

wss.on('connection', (ws) => {
  msgCount.set(ws, 0);

  ws.on('message', (raw) => {
    const count = (msgCount.get(ws) || 0) + 1;
    if (count > 100) { ws.close(1008, 'Rate limited'); return; }
    msgCount.set(ws, count);

    let msg;
    try { msg = JSON.parse(raw); } catch { ws.close(1003, 'Invalid JSON'); return; }

    // Validate schema (e.g. with Zod)
    const result = MessageSchema.safeParse(msg);
    if (!result.success) { ws.close(1003, 'Invalid message'); return; }
  });

  ws.on('close', () => msgCount.delete(ws));
});
```

## 5. Additional Measures

- Set `maxPayload` limits to prevent memory exhaustion
- Implement heartbeat ping/pong to detect zombie connections
- Use `helmet` equivalent settings on HTTP upgrade response
- Log all connection events for audit trails

